@@ -64,6 +64,25 @@ The message is for people; clients branch on `code`.
 `priority` is optional (`normal`). Answers 201 with the new ticket, whose status is `open`. The requester is notified
 that the ticket was received.
 
+### Import tickets: `POST /tickets/import`
+
+```json
+{ "tickets": [
+  { "title": "VPN drops every hour", "requester": "maria@example.com", "priority": "high" },
+  { "title": "Printer jams", "requester": "li@example.com" }
+] }
+```
+
+Each item is what `POST /tickets` takes. At most 5000 items. Creates them in the given order, all of them, or none when
+any item is invalid: then 400 `invalid`, and the message names the first invalid item by its index in the array (0 for
+the first). On success, 201:
+
+```json
+{ "created": 2, "ids": ["T-0001", "T-0002"] }
+```
+
+Each imported ticket is recorded and its requester is notified just as when one ticket is created.
+
 ### List tickets: `GET /tickets`
 
 | Parameter | Meaning |
